  "id": "COMPOUND:16639 - PROTEIN:1493",
  "verbalization": "Estriol-16-Glucuronide is implicated in the biological pathway leading to the Prostaglandin E2 receptor EP4 subtype through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Estriol-16-Glucuronide acts as a target of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4, which in turn is targeted by DL-dimyristoylphosphatidylglycerol and Abiesadine J. These molecules are likely involved in the regulation of the EP4 receptor, which is a key player in inflammatory and physiological processes. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Estriol-16-Glucuronide may influence the EP4 receptor through its interaction with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4, possibly modulating receptor activity or signaling. The evidence supports a role for Estriol-16-Glucuronide in the regulation of the EP4 receptor, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
